 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Decenas y centenas",
    "@en": "Tens and hundreds"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para formar 11–19, di **on** (diez) y luego la unidad: **on bir** (11), **on iki** (12), **on dokuz** (19).",
     "@en": "To form 11-19, di **on** (ten) and then the unit: **on bir** (11), **on iki** (12), **on dokuz** (19)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Las decenas son palabras propias: **yirmi, otuz, kırk, elli, altmış, yetmiş, seksen, doksan**. Se combinan sin «y»: **kırk iki** (42).",
     "@en": "The tens are their own words: **yirmi, otuz, kırk, elli, altmış, yetmiş, seksen, doksan**. They are combined without «y»: **kırk iki** (42)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Yüz** significa cien; **iki yüz** = doscientos.",
     "@en": "**Yüz** means 100; **iki yüz** = 200."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Plural y cantidad",
    "@en": "Plural and quantity"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "El sufijo plural es **-lar/-ler**: **kitaplar** (libros), **evler** (casas). La vocal cambia por armonía.",
     "@en": "The plural suffix is **-lar/-ler**: **kitaplar** (books), **evler** (houses). The vowel changes to harmony."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Después de un número, el nombre suele quedarse en singular: **üç kitap** = tres libros, no *üç kitaplar*.",
     "@en": "After a number, the name is usually left in singular: **üç kitap** = three books, no * üç kitaplar *."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
